around 'Bakool': chema.org/Continent"><a itemprop="url" href="/en/africa/"><span itemprop="name">Africa</span></a></span></div> <div id="social"></div> </div> <header class="cpage"> <a href="javascript:openMap()"><img id="smap" alt="Somalia Map" src="/images/smaps/somalia-cities.png"></a> <h1 itemprop="name">Somalia</h1> <p itemprop="description">Federal Republic of Somalia</p> <span itemprop="geo" itemscope="" itemtype="http://schema.org/GeoCoordinates"><meta itemprop="latitude" content="5.56" /><meta itemprop="longitude" content="45.4"></span> </header> <article class="cpage swapped"> <script>handleArticleResize()</script> <p class="info">The <strong>central government</strong> controls Somalia only partly. <strong>Militant groups</strong> occupy some parts of the country. <strong><a href="../somaliland/admin">Somaliland</a></strong> with the five north-western regions declared independence from Somalia in 1991. Despite of its de-facto independence, it is still internationally considered to be part of Somalia.</p> <section id="adminareas"> <h2>Federal States</h2> <p>The federal states (without Somaliland and without Banaadir that remains a region) consist of following pre-war regions:<ul> <li><strong>Galmudugh</strong>: Galgaduud and southern parts of Mudug.</li> <li><strong>Hirshabelle</strong>: Hiiraan and Shabeellaha Dhexe.</li> <li><strong>Jubaland</strong>: Gedo, Jubbada Dhexe and Jubbada Hoose.</li> <li><strong>Koonfur Galbeed [South West]</strong>: Bakool, Bay and Shabeellaha Hoose.</li> <li><strong>Puntland</strong>: Bari, Nugaal and northern parts of Mudug. It claims also the eastern districts of Somaliland.</li></ul> <h2>Pre-war Regions</h2> <p>The population of the pre-war regions of Somalia according to latest estimates and calculations.</p></p> <table id="tl" class="data"> <thead> <tr id="tlh"><th class="ri" data-coltype
